TITLE:: MapperMap
summary:: one element of a controller moving one target
categories:: Libraries>Mapper
related:: Classes/Mapper, Classes/MapperTarget

DESCRIPTION::
What a mapping does. Made by link::Classes/Mapper#-map::, changed through its setters, and
written out by link::#-asCode::.

code::
m = Mapper.default.map(\m1, \kn_1_1, [\tidal, \cut], 200, 4000);
m.curve = \exp;
m.takeover = \jump;
m.out(0.5);
m.asCode;
::

The element's 0..1 goes through the curve, then from code::lo:: to code::hi:: along the target's
own warp. With code::\pickup:: nothing moves until the element reaches the value the target has
- after the mapping is made, and after anything else moved the target.

A button on an on/off target flips it (code::\toggle::) or holds it while down
(code::\momentary::); on a trigger it fires; on anything else it flips between lo and hi or holds
hi while down. A knob on an on/off target turns it on above the middle.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: lo
Where the element's bottom sends the target, in the target's own units. Until one is set it is
the bottom of the target's range, whatever that is when asked.

METHOD:: hi
The same for the top. Under lo turns the control round.

METHOD:: curve
code::\lin::, code::\exp::, code::\log::, code::\scurve::, a Number (lincurve's curve) or an Env
from 0 to 1.

METHOD:: invert

METHOD:: takeover
code::\pickup:: or code::\jump::.

METHOD:: mode
code::\toggle:: or code::\momentary::.

METHOD:: target
RETURNS:: its link::Classes/MapperTarget::

METHOD:: ktl
The controller's name.

METHOD:: element
The element's name.

METHOD:: isWaiting
Whether its target is not there now.

METHOD:: isCaught
Whether the element has picked the target up.

METHOD:: shape
0..1 through the curve.

METHOD:: out
Where 0..1 of the element sends the target, in its units.

METHOD:: lastInput
The element's last value.

METHOD:: asCode
The line that makes it again.
ARGUMENT:: receiver
what the line calls map on
ARGUMENT:: address
the target as that receiver names it

METHOD:: label
